				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<div class="elementor-image-box-wrapper"><figure class="elementor-image-box-img"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="333" src="https://7statespestcontrol.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pharaohant.jpeg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-image-1222" alt="Coastal Brown Ants" srcset="https://7statespestcontrol.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pharaohant.jpeg 500w, https://7statespestcontrol.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pharaohant-300x200.jpeg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /></figure><div class="elementor-image-box-content"><h3 class="elementor-image-box-title">4. Coastal Brown Ants</h3><p class="elementor-image-box-description">Coastal brown ants, also known as big-headed ants, are commonly found in outdoor areas but can invade homes. They build nests in soil, walls, and pavements, often forming extensive colonies that are difficult to manage without expert intervention.</p></div></div>				</div>
